      },
      "message": "fix(motion): the corner check reads a cusp loop that crosses itself\n\nconnected_pieces built the fill of each outer loop with Region::new.\nThe loops come from a boolean (a piece less its swept area). A bore\ndrawn as chords leaves a cusp a few microns wide at each chord vertex,\nand the boolean can return such a cusp as one loop that crosses itself.\nRegion::new refused it, so the whole corner check stopped with\n\"invalid geometry: loop crosses itself\".\n\nRead each loop with Region::from_slices (the even-odd reading). The\nnoise filters then drop the cusp as before. A loop that does not cross\nitself gives the same region.\n\nPinned by machining2d::unreached::law::\na_chord_cusp_that_crosses_itself_does_not_stop_the_corner_check, which\nfails on main with a synthetic 25 mm bore.\n\nPartial: the three toolpath tests of the issue have other causes and\nneed PR B of #917.\n\nRefs #2849\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
